  "published": "2026-10-07T11:26:34.703Z",
  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Adds optional logging, tracing, metrics, and conversation health signals: ConversationConfigBuilder.WithLoggerFactory(ILoggerFactory), plus an ActivitySource and a Meter named TokenGuard. Fixes pinned-message placement, tool-loop compaction, turn grouping, and option validation.\n\nBehavior changes, with no signature changes: PrepareResult.TokensAfterCompaction includes the provider correction and can turn a Ready or Compacted result into CompactionInsufficient or CannotCompact; Build() rejects NaN thresholds and default-constructed option structs; prepared views place pinned messages relative to their neighbours, keep the user message that opened a tool loop, and group turns by message structure.\n\nKnown limits: the token counter, summarizer, summary formatter, and builder registration of a custom compaction strategy are closed to consumers; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas; the package targets net10.0 only.\n\nFull details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
